how to start a team with no funds so I  got a great question for one of my  YouTube viewers love you guys hand done  by the diva who wrote in to say great  Vidhan I listen at you quite often  you've helped me understand so much I  have a question and comment actually I  have a handmade Julie business and I  need help with branding and marketing I  really don't know who to turn to for  help with making my items because I'm  the only one who knows what I really  want to be made however I want to start  a team that helped me build my business  and even help them build themselves in  the process I currently do it all and I  don't have the funds to pay anyone as of  right now hopefully soon but I don't  want to get burned out either any  suggestions thanks in advance so  handmade by the diva you are in a common  situation a lot of entrepreneurs face  you're working 80 hundred hours a week  trying to create this thing trying to  get it launched you're not getting  momentum you're feeling overwhelmed  overburdened you're gonna get burned out  going this way you're gonna get burned  out and successful entrepreneurs are the  ones who can build beyond themselves so  you are asking the right questions how  do I start building this team now you're  thinking bigger picture because this has  to be beyond just you so I'm gonna give  you three strategies for how you can  build your business up get a team on  without using your big funds okay number  one get a partner the most important  thing that you need to figure out when  you're building a team is what are you  gonna bring to the company right what  are your biggest strengths where should  you be focusing and then you're bringing  people on to complement all the areas  that you're weak at or don't want to do  I call that CEO time right where are you  spending your CEO time the stuff where  you're adding so much value to your  business that's where you need to focus  almost all your efforts and delegate  automate eliminate everything else so if  you're gonna bring a partner on board  you got to think are you best at making  the jewelry or marketing it and it  sounds like you're best at making this  stuff right you're you're reluctant to  give up control of that but you're  struggling with the marketing and  branding so an option is to bring on a  part  the business who doesn't want to make  the jewelry but wants to focus on  marketing Branden I love that stuff and  lives that stuff it eats and breathes  that stuff right somebody who loves  marketing and branding just as much as  you love making jewelry and you bring  that person on as a partner in the  business and how you work it out it's up  to you if they're gonna be 50/50  partners or they're gonna be a smaller  percentage because you've already  started this business I would start them  off in increments because you don't want  just give up a chunk of your equity and  that's gone forever right make them  prove themselves when they can do this  much for you when you've shown that you  guys can work together then they get 10%  of your company and then they get to  this point they get 20% and the next  point they get 30% make them earn in or  they could buy in and give you money for  so it's two different options doesn't  cost you money out of the gate it is an  expensive long term solution because  you've lost a chunk of your company but  if you bring on the right person who you  can work really well with who has the  same values as you and who can bring a  lot of benefit to your business then  they can more than pay for itself so  number one is get a partner number two  is get an intern and this is where you  find a college or high school student to  come in and work under you you said you  wanted to build a team and so that they  could build themselves up as well  so it sounds like you're the kind of  person who likes giving back who wants  to see people do better and get better  and that's a great mentality to go into  as someone who's gonna be a boss because  you're not just saying do this do this  do this do this you're actually trying  to improve them and help them grow so if  you want to get help on making the  designs and making the jewelry well  you're gonna focus on the the marketing  and the branding then you can have a  high school or college intern come in  and you can teach them right you can  still come with the design but you can  eliminate some of the actual making of  it by teaching somebody else how to do  it and they're gonna get better and  they're gonna get stronger and they're  gonna maybe come up with some ideas that  may surprise you as well the high school  interns typically are free because  they're doing it just for school credit  and they have to show up because they  want to get the grade for their school  the university interns are mixed some of  them are free some of them are paid  depends on the program but still very  affordable compared  to hiring somebody on a full-time job so  check out your local schools and see if  there might be a potential fit to have  somebody come in and help you make the  jewelry and number three is hire  somebody part-time a lot of people think  oh I don't have the money to afford send  me to come work in my business but you  don't have to hire someone full-time it  could be on a part-time basis the first  person I hired was for one hour a day  and that freed up more than one hour  over they of my time because he was  better at what he did then then I could  do it I wasn't a huge outpouring of  capital right I didn't have a lot of  money when I was starting at my business  so I couldn't afford to bring on  somebody full-time even part-time but  like one hour a day I could afford that  and that freed up some of my time and so  it encouraged you to look at can you  bring somebody on even for one hour a  day it may be a friend and maybe a  family member I'd also looked to  websites like odesk.com  I'm a big fan of oDesk and you can find  people from around the world with tons  of skills who can help you maybe not do  the actual jewelry because you need  somebody maybe local but they can help  you with your marketing and your  branding or maybe your admin work or  maybe the the stuff that you hate doing  in your business that that you still  have to get done but can be outsourced  to somebody overseas just get that  mentality where you can go out and hire  somebody for as little as an hour a day  or a couple hours a week just to leave  e8 some of the burden off of your  shoulder so you can focus on the higher  value stuff for your business and not  have to spend a ton of money for that  person to come in and help you  so in summary number one get a partner  number two get an intern number three  hire somebody part-time believe for  those of you watching like this video  you can support me by clicking on the  link in the description leave a comment  below let me know what you think ask a  question and click on my face to  subscribe to the channel thank you so  much I'll see you soon
 

